From: fanboy <fanboy@openwrt.org>
Date: Mon, 09 Nov 2026 19:37:44 -1000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: cfg80211: pass the net namespace to wireless_nlevent_flush()

Kernel 7.4-rc2 changed wireless_nlevent_flush() to take the network
namespace whose queued events are to be flushed, and to flush only that
namespace (include/net/iw_handler.h:417, net/wireless/wext-core.c:345 of
linux-7.4-rc2). The in-tree cfg80211 netdev notifier calls
wireless_nlevent_flush(dev_net(dev)) accordingly
(net/wireless/core.c:1946).

backports-7.2 still calls the no-argument variant from
cfg80211_netdev_notifier_call(), which fails to compile against the 7.4
headers ("too few arguments to function 'wireless_nlevent_flush'").
Call it with dev_net(dev) behind LINUX_VERSION_IS_GEQ(7,4,0) to match
the in-tree code, keeping the no-argument call for older kernels.

net/wireless/core.c is the only compiled object referencing the function
in this configuration: CONFIG_WEXT_CORE and CPTCFG_CFG80211_WEXT are
both unset, so backports wext-core.o and wext-compat.o/wext-sme.o are
not built.

Signed-off-by: fanboy <fanboy@openwrt.org>
---
 net/wireless/core.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/net/wireless/core.c
+++ b/net/wireless/core.c
@@ -1864,7 +1864,11 @@ static int cfg80211_netdev_notifier_call
 		return NOTIFY_DONE;
 	}
 
+#if LINUX_VERSION_IS_GEQ(7,4,0)
+	wireless_nlevent_flush(dev_net(dev));
+#else
 	wireless_nlevent_flush();
+#endif
 
 	return NOTIFY_OK;
 }
